{"format":"nexus-update-v1","version":"2.3.0","notes":"Nexus 2.3.0: talk to the orb without opening anything\n\n- Mini chat under the orb: type in the small \"Ask Nexus\" bar or press its mic. The answer pops up in a bubble above the orb and is read out loud, and the big panel stays closed. Click the bubble to open the full chat.\n- Say \"Nexus\" anywhere: \"Nexus, open Blender\", \"what should I work on next, Nexus\" and it just does it. Saying only \"Nexus\" starts listening. Turn it on in Settings > Assistant > Say \"Nexus\". It runs offline with Windows speech, and the orb ignores its own voice.\n- The empty space around the orb is click-through, so it never blocks what's behind it.\n- The orb's bar shows what's going on: waiting permissions, agents working, thinking, speaking.","payload":"","signature":"Cylb3Uy/yoxPM3FyjLK3wUX48/QX+Z+0xvuZJdZ+b7U3C2/XHCyH+RW6xsvg6phgwf5gFUK/2JfEMhRLJFQ6CA=="}